Given a 2D square matrix mat[][] of size n x n, rotate it by 180 degrees without using extra space.

Note: You must rotate the matrix in place and modify the input matrix directly.

Examples:

Input:  mat[][] = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]
Output: [[9, 8, 7], [6, 5, 4], [3, 2, 1]]
Explanation:

The output matrix is the input matrix rotated by 180 degress.
 

Input: mat[][] = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
Output: [[4, 3], [2, 1]]
Explanation : The output matrix is the input matrix rotated by 180 degrees.


class Solution {
    public void rotateMatrix(int[][] mat) {
        rotate90(mat);
        rotate90(mat);
    }
    private void rotate90(int[][] mat){
    int n =mat.length;
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
            int temp=mat[i][j];
            mat[i][j]=mat[j][i];
            mat[j][i]=temp;
        }
    }
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        int left=0;
        int right=n-1;
        while(left<right){
            int temp=mat[i][left];
            mat[i][left]=mat[i][right];
            mat[i][right]=temp;
            left++;
            right--;
        }
    }
  }
}

